## Mobile first

Design and implement for **phone first**, desktop second. See [.cursor/rules/mobile-first.mdc](mobile-first.mdc).

## Visual defaults

- Full-bleed hero (video or still), generous whitespace, restrained type.
- Sticky nav: Info · Offerings · Memberships · New here (reserved — no Buy/Reserve/Member on marketing). See [.cursor/rules/todd-nav-preferences.mdc](todd-nav-preferences.mdc).
- Repeated journey CTA → `/new-here`.
- Footer: address, segmented emails (info / membership / training), social, legal, optional newsletter.
- `/buy`, `/schedule`, `/account`: site header/footer only; minimal chrome around gym-software embed.

## Feature defaults

- Marketing on Next.js + Firebase; booking/credits/account via **gym software embed** (no custom member auth or billing in v1).
- Sukha-style membership application; **no public monthly prices** unless the brand kit marks pricing as approved.
- No apparel shop in v1 unless brand kit changelog says otherwise.

## When assets are approved

Append fonts, colors, logo paths, and copy tone to [docs/brand/united-strength-aesthetic.md](../docs/brand/united-strength-aesthetic.md) with a changelog entry. Mirror values in Tailwind/theme config. Do not hardcode one-off brand values only in components.

Store files under `public/brand/` when the app exists; record path and usage in the brand kit.

## Anti-patterns

- Busy multi-banner nav, lorem ipsum at launch.
- Rebuilding Mariana Tek / Mindbody booking, credits, or waitlists in custom code.
- Ethos-style public tier cards without explicit client sign-off in the brand kit.
